Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser, python3 (>= 3.12), python3-yaml, python3-cryptography, openssh-client, wireguard-tools, iproute2, maluos-firstboot (>= 0.1.10), maluos-vault (>= 0.4.1)
Recommends: maluos-gateway (>= 0.4.2)
Description: MaluOS estate membership: maluctl estate and the node heartbeat
 A MaluOS server joins its estate the way a desk joins an office (Phase 13
 slice 1, docs/phase13-slice1-nodes.md): `sudo maluctl estate join URL
 --code CODE` exchanges a one-time node code for a node token, keeps the
 token and an ed25519 node key in the vault in the host principal's
 compartment (host:<hostname>, stored as the system user maluos-estate),
 records the office and its endpoints in /etc/maluos/estate.yaml, and
 starts maluos-estate.service, which heartbeats the office with the
 machine's facts and, every report_s, the report an operator needs: units,
 agents, the gateway, vault alerts, updates, disk, memory and load.
 .
 `maluctl estate status|report|nodes|leave`. A desk does not enrol twice:
 its desk row is its node record, and `maluctl estate nodes` on a desk
 shows the estate as its owner may see it. The package also carries the
 shared estate client (maluos_estate.client) and the mock office tests use.
 .
 The overlay (slice 1b): the join makes the host's WireGuard key, the
 office gives it an address and a name on the estate's own network, and
 maluos-overlay.service keeps the tunnel to the hub (or, on the hub, to
 every spoke) and the names in /etc/hosts (NAME.internal). `maluctl estate
 overlay status|peers|up|down|rotate|refresh`.
